window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-7ad4400e7f60343d"]={"key":"ny_b1-7ad4400e7f60343d","group":"ny_b1","uid":"7ad4400e7f60343d","rank":23,"title":"cavendish press quarterly restore verification","occupation":"computer_information_systems_managers","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You’re the information systems manager overseeing the hosting transition for Cavendish Press. Yewbank Foundry took over the hosted publishing environment three weeks ago, and operations director Jasmin Castellanos needs to run and sign off the next quarterly restore drill herself before the December issue cycle. Jasmin has no technical staff reporting to her, while the peer who will review the completed record is technically experienced, so the document has to work for both readers without becoming a backup-technology tutorial. Please create `quarterly_restore_verification.docx` and write it into the top level of the working directory using exactly that filename. Keep the complete document to no more than six pages, including the procedure, comparison, evidence record and sign-off space. It needs to be reusable every quarter rather than written as a one-off report. Please make sure it (1) gives Jasmin a practical procedure she can execute from preparation through final sign-off without having to ask what an instruction means, while making clear where she must stop and obtain help rather than improvise; (2) lets her record the recovery point, elapsed times, checks performed, evidence retained, exceptions and final result without inventing environment details, credentials, contacts or measurements that we have not supplied; (3) restates the 24-hour recovery point objective and four-hour recovery time objective as things she can personally observe and assess during the drill; (4) includes a plain two-period comparison explaining the material difference between Elena Asante’s June record and the current-quarter rehearsal; (5) distinguishes recovery of an individual file from verification that the hosted publishing service is usable; and (6) finishes with a sign-off that makes the outcome and any unresolved exception unambiguous to Jasmin and the technical peer reviewer. For the comparison, Elena’s June sheet marked the drill “Pass” and recorded 58 minutes after one document was recovered from the former standalone nightly full backup. It did not record the assumed interruption time, the backup timestamp, what started or stopped the timer, or any application-level checks. In the current-quarter rehearsal, the assumed interruption was 08:30 on 2 December and the selected recovery point was 23:00 on 1 December. The first requested file was available at 09:42, and access to the restored publishing application plus completion of the recorded validation checks occurred at 13:18. The new hosted design uses a Sunday full backup followed by daily incrementals, and its dashboard showed the relevant backup jobs as successful. People here commonly take a successful backup-job indicator as proof that a restore will work, but the move to an incremental chain and an application-level drill is exactly the setting in which that shorthand may not be enough. Explain the difference without claiming that June met an objective its record could not demonstrate, and without presenting a longer current-quarter figure as proof that hosting performance deteriorated. Use only the objectives, dates, times and historical facts given here for populated results; leave reusable fields clearly available for quarter-specific operational details. Do not include vendor-console click paths or production credentials. The final document should be concise enough to use during an out-of-hours event, but it must still leave an auditable record of what was actually verified.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `quarterly_restore_verification.docx` — Reusable quarterly restore-verification procedure, evidence record, two-period comparison and sign-off for Cavendish Press. (Must be written at the top level of the working directory using the exact filename quarterly_restore_verification.docx; must be no more than six rendered pages; must remain editable and must not contain vendor-console click paths or production credentials.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/quarterly_restore_verification.docx","bytes":41687,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/e2e428dd59cbf0ffc15d801059334e4fd7d138558171d0cdb5f70db392f821b2.docx","sha256":"e2e428dd59cbf0ffc15d801059334e4fd7d138558171d0cdb5f70db392f821b2","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"CAVENDISH PRESS\nQuarterly Restore-Verification Procedure\nOwner: Information Systems Manager | Operator: Jasmin Castellanos, Operations Director | Use: scheduled quarterly drill only\nPurpose and boundary. Verify recovery of the hosted publishing service in an authorised, isolated/non-production destination. This is a planned exercise, not authority to alter the live publishing environment during an outage. Do not overwrite, attach, or promote the test restore into production without separate written authorisation.\n1. Pre-drill checklist (complete before timing starts)\nCheck\nRecord / action\nAuthorisation\nDrill approval reference: ____________________   Test destination approved: Yes / No\nWindow and notice\nApproved window (date/time/time zone): ____________________   Operational parties notified: Yes / No / N/A\nAccess\nTest login/access to backup and isolated destination succeeds before timed restore. Credentials remain outside this document. Result: Pass / Fail\nCapacity\nFree storage/capacity checked against intended restore scope: Pass / Fail   Evidence ref: __________\nScope\nPublishing service/application: ____________________   Representative file/content: ____________________\nSource and destination\nFull/base backup ID or label: __________   Required incremental IDs (all through point): __________   Isolated destination: __________\nRecovery point\nSelect and record the exact recovery-point timestamp before restore: __________ (time zone: ________). Do not substitute an undocumented point.\nStop and obtain help from the designated technical support role if authorisation, access, capacity, destination identity, or any chain member is missing, unreadable, out of order, or uncertain. Never skip a chain member or improvise a substitute. Preserve the observed message, IDs, timestamps, screenshots/logs, attempted steps and current state for escalation.\n2. Objectives and timing rules\nRPO (24 hours) is the maximum acceptable age of recovered data at the assumed interruption: calculate interruption timestamp minus the timestamp of the recovery point actually restored. RTO (4 hours) is the maximum uninterrupted elapsed time from the defined recovery start to a usable, checked publishing service. First-file availability is a separate milestone and does not stop the RTO timer.\nTiming field\nRule / quarter record\nClock convention\nUse one stated clock and time zone for every timestamp. Time zone: __________   Clock/source: __________\nRTO start\nStart at the assumed interruption time (or an explicitly authorised recovery-start time if the drill record says so). Start: __________\nFirst file\nRecord when the first requested file becomes available; keep timer running. First-file time: __________\nRTO stop\nStop only after application access plus every required validation in section 3 is complete. Stop: __________\nElapsed calculations\nRPO age = interruption - recovery point: __________ (objective \u003c= 24:00; Pass / Fail). RTO = stop - start: __________ (objective \u003c= 4:00; Pass / Fail).\nRetries/pauses\nKeep the RTO timer running through failed attempts, retries and technical pauses. Log every attempt/restart below; do not reset the start.\n3. Execute, validate and retain evidence\nAfter the pre-drill checks, start at the recorded boundary, restore to the isolated destination, and log each attempt. For the hosted design, confirm the Sunday full backup followed by daily incrementals, including every applicable incremental through the selected point; confirm completeness and order before relying on the chain. A successful dashboard job indicator proves job completion status only; it does not prove end-to-end restorability. That shorthand stops being sufficient when a restore depends on a base plus incrementals and the endpoint is a usable application.\nValidation (all required)\nResult (Pass / Fail / Not tested / Exception) and evidence/notes\nOpen/access restored publishing application in isolated environment\nResult: ______   Evidence ref: ______________________________\nOpen representative restored content and confirm readable (not merely present)\nResult: ______   Item: __________   Evidence: __________________\nConfirm linked assets/images/attachments remain available\nResult: ______   Evidence: ______________________________\nRun representative search/index lookup/retrieval\nResult: ______   Query/content: __________   Evidence: __________\nCheck expected access permissions/role restrictions (allowed and denied as appropriate)\nResult: ______   Evidence: ______________________________\nProduce representative preview/export/rendering relevant to publishing\nResult: ______   Output ref: ______________________________\nIntegrity/completeness check: expected count, checksum, provider verification or reconciled sample\nExpected: ______   Restored: ______   Method/evidence: __________\nAttempt / event log\nStart\nEnd / milestone\nOutcome / evidence\n1\n__________\n__________\n________________________________\n2 / retry\n__________\n__________\n________________________________\n3 / other\n__________\n__________\n________________________________\n4. Result, exceptions and closeout\nRecord every failed or not-tested check as an exception; do not replace it with a general Pass. Overall status rule: an RPO miss, RTO miss, incomplete chain, failed mandatory validation, or unresolved safety/technical uncertainty cannot be an unqualified Pass. Use Pass, Pass with exception, Fail, or Incomplete and explain why.\nObjective / result\nMeasured value\nAssessment\nRPO (\u003c= 24 hours)\n________________\nPass / Fail / Incomplete\nRTO (\u003c= 4 hours)\n________________\nPass / Fail / Incomplete\nOverall drill status\n________________\nPass / Pass with exception / Fail / Incomplete\nException or corrective action\nOwner (role/name)\nTarget date\nClosed / evidence ref\n________________________________\n________________\n____________\n________________\n________________________________\n________________\n____________\n________________\nBefore cleanup, retain the completed record and evidence references (backup/job IDs, chain IDs, restore IDs, screenshots, logs, validation outputs and ticket/change references) in the organisation's approved operational record for later technical peer review. Only after evidence is retained and release is authorised, clean up the isolated restore and drill-created data. Never delete or modify production material.\n5. Two-period comparison (June vs current-quarter rehearsal)\nPeriod\nWhat was recorded\nWhat it proves / does not prove\nJune - Elena Asante\nMarked Pass; 58 minutes after one document was recovered from the former standalone nightly full backup. No assumed interruption time, backup timestamp, timer start/stop boundary, or application-level checks recorded.\nA single-file recovery duration from a standalone full backup. The record cannot demonstrate 24-hour RPO or four-hour RTO compliance, so June must not be treated as objective evidence.\nCurrent-quarter rehearsal\nAssumed interruption 08:30 on 2 December; selected recovery point 23:00 on 1 December. First file available 09:42; restored publishing application accessible and recorded validation complete 13:18. Hosted design: Sunday full plus daily incrementals; relevant dashboard jobs successful.\nRPO age = 9h 30m (08:30 minus 23:00) -> meets 24h. First-file milestone = 1h 12m (08:30 to 09:42), not RTO endpoint. RTO = 4h 48m (08:30 to 13:18) -> misses 4h by 48m.\nThe figures are materially different in scope and measurement: June timed one document from a standalone nightly full backup, while the rehearsal timed a chained hosted restore through application-level usability checks. The longer current-quarter figure therefore does not by itself show that hosting performance deteriorated. It shows a more complete endpoint and a dependency chain whose successful-job indicators still require restore and service validation.\n6. Sign-off\nDecision record\nEntry\nOperator statement\nI confirm the recorded steps, timestamps, evidence and exceptions are accurate to the drill performed. Operator: ____________________  Date/time: __________  Decision: __________\nTechnical peer review\nI reviewed the record and evidence references. Peer reviewer: ____________________  Date/time: __________  Acknowledgment: Accept / Return for correction\nUnresolved exception at sign-off\nNone / See corrective-action row(s): ____________________   Owner and target date recorded: Yes / No\nFinal outcome must state RPO and RTO separately. For this current-quarter rehearsal: RPO met; RTO not met; overall status is not eligible for an unqualified Pass.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required DOCX exists under the exact filename quarterly_restore_verification.docx and opens as a valid, editable Word document.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"quarterly_restore_verification.docx","grader_hint":"Confirm the exact filename, parse the DOCX package and verify that substantive content is editable rather than supplied only as page images."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The complete rendered document is no more than six pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered quarterly_restore_verification.docx","grader_hint":"Render the document using a standard office renderer and count all pages, including comparison, record and sign-off content."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies itself as a quarterly restore-verification procedure for Cavendish Press.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Document title or opening identification","grader_hint":"Look for a clear title or opening statement containing Cavendish Press, quarterly frequency and restore verification."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document is written so Jasmin Castellanos can execute it while a technically experienced peer can review the resulting evidence, without turning the document into a general backup tutorial.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole document","grader_hint":"Judge whether instructions are plain and operational, technical terms are explained only as needed, and the content remains concise and professionally useful to both audiences."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The procedure has a clear, navigable execution flow from preparation through result determination and sign-off.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Procedure structure","grader_hint":"Check whether a reader can readily find what to do before, during and after the drill without reconstructing the order from narrative prose."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The scope identifies the exercise as restore verification in an isolated or non-production target rather than restoration over the live publishing environment.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope or safety language","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent language requiring a segregated test destination and protecting the live environment."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure distinguishes a scheduled quarterly verification drill from an actual service-recovery incident.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope, purpose or preparation content","grader_hint":"Look for language preventing the drill procedure from being mistaken for authorization to alter production during a real outage."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The preparation content requires confirmation that the drill and its test destination are authorized before restoration begins.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pre-drill checks","grader_hint":"Confirm that authorization is an explicit precondition, not merely an optional sign-off after the work."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure requires the operator to confirm that the target has sufficient storage or capacity for the intended restore before starting.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pre-drill checks","grader_hint":"Accept a capacity, free-space or target-sizing check tied to the selected restore scope."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure requires access and authentication to be tested before the timed restore starts, without embedding credentials.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pre-drill access checks","grader_hint":"Look for a preflight login or access check and verify that no real or invented password, token or production secret appears."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure requires confirmation of the approved drill window and any necessary notification to affected operational parties.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Preparation content","grader_hint":"Accept role-based notification and window confirmation; named contacts are not required."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The record captures the application or service in scope and the specific data or content selected for verification.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reusable drill record","grader_hint":"Look for fields or prompts that identify both the service and representative restore content."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The record captures the source backup set or recovery set and the destination environment.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reusable drill record","grader_hint":"Accept provider-generated identifiers, labels or locations; both source and destination must be distinguishable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure requires the intended recovery point to be selected and recorded before the restore is initiated.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Preparation and execution instructions","grader_hint":"Check sequencing: selection and recording must occur before the restore action, not be reconstructed only afterward."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure restates the 24-hour RPO as the maximum acceptable age of the recovered data at the assumed interruption time.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Objective explanation","grader_hint":"The plain-language definition must concern data age or potential data loss, not restore duration."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The reusable record supports calculating RPO by comparing the assumed interruption timestamp with the timestamp of the recovery point actually restored.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"RPO fields or formula","grader_hint":"Verify that both timestamps and their elapsed difference can be recorded; a generic RPO pass box alone is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure restates the four-hour RTO as the maximum elapsed time until the restored service reaches the defined usable and verified state.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Objective explanation","grader_hint":"The definition must extend beyond the appearance of the first restored file and identify a usable, checked service endpoint."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure defines and records a reproducible RTO start event tied to the assumed interruption or authorized recovery start.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timing instructions and record","grader_hint":"Look for one explicit timing boundary that another operator could apply consistently; vague wording such as 'when work begins' is inadequate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure defines and records an RTO stop event that occurs only after required application-level validation is complete.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timing instructions and record","grader_hint":"Confirm that data copy completion, mount completion or first-file access alone cannot stop the RTO timer."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The reusable record supports calculating measured RTO as the uninterrupted elapsed time between the defined start and stop timestamps.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"RTO fields or formula","grader_hint":"Verify that start, stop and elapsed duration can all be documented and reconciled."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document instructs the operator to use one stated clock and time zone for all drill timestamps.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timing convention","grader_hint":"Accept a field for time zone plus an instruction to use a consistent time source."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The record separately captures the time the first requested file becomes available and the time the restored service becomes usable and verified.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timing record","grader_hint":"Both milestones must be separately labeled so the file-recovery duration cannot be mistaken for RTO."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure keeps the RTO timer running through failed attempts, retries or technical pauses unless the documented objective explicitly allows exclusion.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timing or exception instructions","grader_hint":"Look for a rule preventing a retry from silently resetting the measured recovery time."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The record captures every restore attempt or restart with its timing and outcome.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Attempt or event log","grader_hint":"Accept a repeatable event log or clearly reusable rows for attempts, including unsuccessful ones."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"For an incremental design, the procedure requires identification of the applicable full backup and every required incremental through the selected recovery point.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Backup-set verification instructions","grader_hint":"Look for the full base plus ordered dependent incrementals; referring generically to 'the latest backup' is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure requires the chain's completeness and order to be checked before relying on it for the restore.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Backup-chain verification instructions","grader_hint":"Confirm that missing, inaccessible or out-of-sequence chain members are treated as a material condition rather than ignored."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document states that successful backup-job indicators establish job completion status but do not by themselves prove end-to-end restorability.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Procedure guidance or comparison explanation","grader_hint":"The wording may be plain, but it must preserve the distinction between a green job status and a verified usable restore."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies when the successful-job rule of thumb stops being sufficient: where recovery depends on a base backup, subsequent incrementals and application-level usability checks.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Procedure guidance or comparison explanation","grader_hint":"Require a concrete applicability boundary tied to chained dependencies and the service-level endpoint, not a generic statement that restores should sometimes be tested."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A missing, unreadable or unverifiable chain member triggers a stop or escalation rather than an instruction to skip that member or choose an undocumented substitute.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Stop and escalation rules","grader_hint":"Accept defensible role-based escalation language; the operator must not be told to improvise around a chain gap."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure prohibits overwriting, attaching or promoting the test restore into production without separate authorization.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Safety or stop conditions","grader_hint":"Look for an explicit production-protection boundary, not merely a preference to use a test system."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure includes a stop condition for an unexpected production impact, destination mismatch or risk of overwriting live data.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Stop conditions","grader_hint":"At least one clear instruction must tell Jasmin not to continue if the target or production safety is uncertain."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure verifies that the restored publishing application can be opened or accessed in the test environment.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Application validation checks","grader_hint":"Look for a direct application-access check rather than only confirmation that files exist."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure requires opening representative restored content and confirming that it is readable rather than merely present.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Content validation checks","grader_hint":"Accept a documented sample selected before or during the drill; presence-only checks do not satisfy this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure includes a check that linked assets, images, attachments or equivalent dependent content remain available with the restored item.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Content validation checks","grader_hint":"Look for validation of dependent publishing assets, not solely the primary document."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure includes a representative search, index lookup or retrieval check in the restored application.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Application validation checks","grader_hint":"Accept an equivalent check demonstrating that restored content is retrievable through the application."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure includes a check that expected access permissions or role restrictions remain effective in the restored application.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Application validation checks","grader_hint":"A useful check confirms appropriate allowed or denied access without requiring production credentials in the document."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure includes a representative output, preview, export or rendering check relevant to publishing use.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Application validation checks","grader_hint":"Accept any bounded check demonstrating that the restored application can produce a meaningful publishing output."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure requires an integrity or completeness check whose result is recorded, such as an expected count, checksum, provider verification or reconciled sample.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Data validation and evidence record","grader_hint":"The document need not prescribe one unavailable local value, but it must provide a defensible way to compare expected and restored content."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each required validation check has a recordable result such as pass, fail, not tested or exception, with space for evidence or notes.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Validation record","grader_hint":"Verify that checks are auditable and not presented only as prose instructions with no place to capture outcomes."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The drill record captures evidence references such as job IDs, backup-set IDs, screenshots, logs or ticket references without requiring evidence to be embedded in the procedure.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Evidence record","grader_hint":"Look for reusable reference fields covering both backup and restore evidence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The record captures the operator, drill date, environment and drill or change reference.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Drill identification fields","grader_hint":"All four identification elements must be available as editable fields."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure directs the operator to record exceptions and failed checks when they occur rather than replacing them with a general pass statement.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exception and result instructions","grader_hint":"Look for explicit preservation of exceptions in the final record."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The record provides for each unresolved exception or corrective action to have an owner and target date.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Corrective-action record","grader_hint":"Both responsibility and due date must be recordable; a free-text notes box alone is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure provides a role-based escalation route for technical failure or uncertainty without inventing a named contact.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Escalation instructions","grader_hint":"Accept an editable role or contact field combined with a clear escalation trigger."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Escalation instructions tell the operator what evidence and context to preserve or provide when seeking help.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Escalation instructions","grader_hint":"Look for useful items such as timestamps, IDs, messages, screenshots, attempted steps and observed state."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure includes controlled cleanup of the isolated restore and drill-created data after evidence is retained and release is authorized.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Closeout instructions","grader_hint":"The sequence must preserve evidence before cleanup and avoid implying that the operator may delete production material."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure states where or under what record the completed drill evidence should be retained for later review.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Closeout or retention instruction","grader_hint":"A role-based or system-neutral record location is acceptable; an invented repository name is not required."},{"rubric_item_id":"R48","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The sign-off records RPO and RTO as separate outcomes rather than combining them into a single undifferentiated pass box.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Result and sign-off record","grader_hint":"Verify separate measured values and separate pass/fail or exception determinations for the two objectives."},{"rubric_item_id":"R49","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The overall drill status follows a stated rule under which an objective miss or incomplete mandatory validation cannot be reported as an unqualified pass.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Result logic and sign-off","grader_hint":"Accept clear labels such as pass, pass with exception, fail or incomplete, provided the rule prevents a clean pass when a required objective or check is not met."},{"rubric_item_id":"R50","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The sign-off captures the operator's name, date and decision, and provides a distinct peer-review acknowledgment or review field.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Sign-off block","grader_hint":"The operator and peer-review roles must be distinct even if the peer review occurs later."},{"rubric_item_id":"R51","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The June comparison accurately reports Elena Asante's recorded Pass, the 58-minute figure and recovery of one document from the former standalone nightly full backup.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Two-period comparison","grader_hint":"All supplied June facts must appear without adding unsupported June measurements."},{"rubric_item_id":"R52","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The comparison states that the June record omitted the assumed interruption time, backup timestamp, timer boundaries and application-level validation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Two-period comparison","grader_hint":"All four evidentiary gaps should be identified clearly enough to explain the limit on the June conclusion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R53","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The current-quarter comparison accurately records the assumed interruption at 08:30 on 2 December and the selected recovery point at 23:00 on 1 December.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Two-period comparison or populated current-quarter record","grader_hint":"Check both timestamps and their roles; they must not be transposed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R54","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The current-quarter recovery-point age is stated as 9 hours 30 minutes, within ±1 minute.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Current-quarter RPO calculation","grader_hint":"Calculate the difference from 23:00 on 1 December to 08:30 on 2 December and compare it with the stated result."},{"rubric_item_id":"R55","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The current-quarter RPO is marked as meeting the 24-hour objective because the calculated recovery-point age is no more than 24 hours.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Current-quarter objective assessment","grader_hint":"The measured value, threshold and pass label must agree."},{"rubric_item_id":"R56","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The elapsed time from the 08:30 assumed interruption to first-file availability at 09:42 is stated as 1 hour 12 minutes, within ±1 minute.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Current-quarter timing comparison","grader_hint":"Verify the arithmetic and that this duration is labeled as the first-file milestone, not the final RTO."},{"rubric_item_id":"R57","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The elapsed time from 08:30 to completion of application access and validation at 13:18 is stated as 4 hours 48 minutes, within ±1 minute.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Current-quarter RTO calculation","grader_hint":"Verify arithmetic from the supplied start and validated-service endpoint."},{"rubric_item_id":"R58","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The current-quarter RTO is marked as not meeting the four-hour objective because 4 hours 48 minutes exceeds the objective by 48 minutes, within ±1 minute.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Current-quarter objective assessment","grader_hint":"The duration, threshold, variance and result label must agree."},{"rubric_item_id":"R59","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The comparison explains plainly that the June 58-minute figure and the current-quarter 4-hour-48-minute figure measure materially different scopes and endpoints.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Two-period comparison narrative","grader_hint":"Look for a concise explanation contrasting one-file recovery from a standalone full backup with application-level usability after a chained hosted restore."},{"rubric_item_id":"R60","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The comparison does not claim that June demonstrated compliance with either the 24-hour RPO or four-hour RTO.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Two-period comparison and conclusions","grader_hint":"The document should explicitly limit the June conclusion because the necessary timestamps and timing boundaries were not recorded."},{"rubric_item_id":"R61","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The comparison does not present the longer current-quarter elapsed time as proof of degraded hosting performance and instead attributes the material difference to non-equivalent scope, architecture and measurement boundaries.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Two-period comparison narrative","grader_hint":"Judge whether the explanation is evidence-bounded and avoids an unsupported causal performance claim."},{"rubric_item_id":"R62","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The comparison notes that the hosted design relies on a Sunday full backup followed by daily incrementals and that the relevant dashboard jobs were reported successful.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Two-period comparison","grader_hint":"Both the chain design and green job status must be accurately stated as context, without treating the latter as conclusive verification."},{"rubric_item_id":"R63","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Reusable quarter-specific fields are blank or clearly marked for completion rather than populated with invented contacts, environment names, credentials, identifiers or measurements.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reusable procedure and record fields","grader_hint":"Inspect populated operational details and confirm that only supplied historical facts and objectives are prefilled; labels, role placeholders and example-free blanks are acceptable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R64","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"A nontechnical operator can complete the procedure and reach a defensible result without asking the author a material procedural question.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole document","grader_hint":"Walk through the procedure as Jasmin: check whether inputs, decisions, stop conditions, result rules, evidence capture and sign-off are sufficiently explicit while unavailable local details are handled by fill-in fields."},{"rubric_item_id":"R65","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document is practical to use during an out-of-hours drill, with concise instructions, legible record fields and no reliance on dense uninterrupted prose.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered whole document","grader_hint":"Judge scanability, typography, spacing and whether the execution record can be completed while performing the drill."},{"rubric_item_id":"R66","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Objective values, supplied timestamps, calculated durations and outcome labels remain internally consistent wherever repeated in the procedure, comparison and sign-off.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole document","grader_hint":"Cross-check every repeated 24-hour objective, four-hour objective, 9-hour-30-minute RPO, 1-hour-12-minute file milestone and 4-hour-48-minute RTO, together with their pass or fail labels."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Cavendish Press has recently moved its hosted publishing environment to Yewbank Foundry. Operations director Jasmin Castellanos must be able to conduct and sign off quarterly restore verification without an in-house technical team, while preserving evidence suitable for technical peer review.","difficulty_sources":["Converting RPO and RTO into observable operator actions without changing their technical meaning","Reconciling two periods whose recorded scopes and timing boundaries are not comparable","Designing for a nontechnical operator and technical peer within a six-page limit","Handling incremental-chain dependencies and the limits of successful backup-job indicators","Providing usable local placeholders without inventing unavailable operational facts"],"authoring_plan":{"mode":"instructional","solver_instance":"An information systems manager must author a compact, reusable restore-verification procedure for a nontechnical operations director and a technical peer reviewer.","behaviour_specification":["Translate RPO into a timestamp comparison between the assumed interruption and the recovery point actually restored.","Translate RTO into uninterrupted elapsed time from a defined recovery start boundary through completion of application-level usability validation.","Keep first-file recovery as an informative milestone that does not terminate the RTO timer.","Treat successful backup-job status as evidence of job completion, not proof that the full dependency chain can be restored into a usable service.","For the hosted incremental design, require the Sunday full backup and every applicable daily incremental through the selected recovery point to be identified, ordered and available.","Require an isolated authorized target, production-protection stop conditions, preflight access and capacity checks, evidence capture, exception handling, role-based escalation, controlled cleanup and retained records.","Use application-level validation appropriate to a publishing service: access, representative content readability, dependent assets, retrieval or search, permissions, representative output and integrity or completeness evidence.","Provide independent RPO and RTO outcomes, an overall-status rule, corrective-action ownership and an unambiguous operator and peer-review sign-off.","Use editable blanks for unavailable local environment names, contacts, credentials, IDs and quarter-specific measurements."],"comparison_gold_relationships":["Current-quarter RPO age equals the interval from 23:00 on 1 December to 08:30 on 2 December: 9 hours 30 minutes; it meets the 24-hour objective.","First-file availability elapsed time equals the interval from 08:30 to 09:42: 1 hour 12 minutes; this is not the RTO endpoint.","Current-quarter RTO equals the interval from 08:30 to 13:18: 4 hours 48 minutes; it misses the four-hour objective by 48 minutes.","June's 58-minute result covers recovery of one document from a standalone nightly full backup and lacks the timestamps, timer definitions and application checks needed to substantiate either RPO or RTO compliance.","The material change must be explained through non-equivalent scope, hosted incremental-chain architecture and a more complete validation endpoint, not asserted degradation in hosting performance.","The intended current-quarter verdict is RPO met, RTO not met, with the overall drill not eligible for an unqualified pass."],"imperfections_and_tensions":["The June record contains a plausible Pass label but insufficient evidence for objective compliance.","The current dashboard contains green successful-job indicators that are insufficient to prove end-to-end restorability in a chained design.","The mixed audience requires operational plain language without a lengthy technical tutorial.","The commonly used successful-job shorthand stops being reliable when the selected recovery point depends on a full-plus-incremental chain and the required endpoint is a usable application.","No local console path, contact directory, credential, environment identifier or evidence repository is available; the procedure must close this gap with role-based and editable pre-drill fields rather than invented facts."],"intended_verdict":"A satisfactory artifact is independently executable by Jasmin Castellanos, technically defensible to a peer reviewer, explicit about evidence limits, and internally consistent in concluding that the current RPO passed while the current RTO missed its objective."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"mixed_media_bundle","structure":"required_sections"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"restore_verification_procedure","filename":"quarterly_restore_verification.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"Reusable quarterly restore-verification procedure, evidence record, two-period comparison and sign-off for Cavendish Press.","required":true,"constraints":["Must be written at the top level of the working directory using the exact filename quarterly_restore_verification.docx; must be no more than six rendered pages; must remain editable and must not contain vendor-console click paths or production credentials."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"evaluate_compliance","work_product":"operating_plan","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"professional_judgment"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"computer_information_systems_managers","sector":"professional_scientific_technical_services","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":5.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"domain_expert","reviewer_policy":"A domain-expert reviewer should render and inspect the DOCX, independently recalculate all supplied-period durations, walk the procedure as a nontechnical operator, and verify that backup-chain, timing-boundary, validation, evidence and sign-off controls are both technically sound and usable within the page limit.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No live environment, provider console or local contact directory is supplied, so the document must use role-based and editable placeholders for local operational details. The review can assess procedural correctness and the supplied two-period comparison but cannot execute an actual restore."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:36:39+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:36:39+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:36:39+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:36:39+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['R53', 'R62']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:36:39+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/7ad4400e7f60343d","declared_deliverables":["quarterly_restore_verification.docx"]};
